# Sometimes we may have options that are chained.
# The idea here is basically that there is no new prompt. 
# This (and supporting the first say) is also why Presentation is nullable
For example;
What would you like to drink? {
    ?: Tea {
        ?: with sugar
            Here you go! Tea with sugar!
        ?: with honey
            Here you go! Tea with honey!
    }
    ?: Coffee {
        ?: With cream
            Here you go! Coffee with cream!
        ?: Black
            Plain ol' coffee, just for you!
    }
}
# Tea is our answer, and it immediately spawns another option set. 
# Tea does not become the prompt in this case, we just move on to the next prompt!

# As another thing to consider, options can be chained together without 
# Any intermediate prompt. Working in a similar way;
What would you like to drink? {
    ?: Tea
        :SET drink=tea
    ?: Coffee
        :SET drink=coffee
} {
    ?: With sugar
        :SET mix=sugar
    ?: With milk
        :SET mix=milk
}
Here you go! $drink with $mix!

Moving on...
Pick {
    ?: A
        Nice choice.
    ?: B
} {
    # Should be paired with displaying "Nice choice."
    # While also being an immediate follow-up prompt to B
    ?: X
}

# Now we hit some annoying combinations...
What do you want to drink?
# Wait for some animation, options present *after* handler continues...
# We're not retroactively trying to pause the prompt
:YIELD look_at_menu
{
    ?: Tea
        Here's your tea.
    ?: Coffee
        Here's your coffee.
}

# idk why you would do this, but we need to support it
# Just like the above, we shouldn't have some meaningless need for
# a continue between these, that chained prompt should appear
# with the "what would you like in..." message.
What would you like to drink? {
    ?: Tea
        And what would you like in your tea?
    ?: Coffee
        And what would you like in your coffee?
} {
    ?: Sugar
        Here's that with sugar!
    ?: Milk
        Here's that with milk!
}

# Other edge case...
Pick {
    ?: A
        Nice choice.
    ?: B
} 
:YIELD some:bullshit
{
    # Should be paired with displaying "Nice choice."
    # While also being an immediate follow-up prompt to B
    ?: X
}

Hello
:SET test=false
{
    ?: [when:test=true] lksdfjklsfd
     ...
}

Do you want any sugar?
# Timing doesn't matter perfectly, do this while rendering the options
:SIGNAL pan_camera_to_coffee_cup
{
    ?: Yes
        ...
    ? No
        ...
}